 "about": "Batch 26 (11 Nov 2026), registered before its scores: the trials, and the floors. Every arm is batch 25's fix1 recipe (the live trees with the expected-time table, one seed) on the same feature cache, with the expected-time table REBUILT: it now reads the trial runs data.clean drops (the audit of 11 Nov, findings 1 to 3) and its trouble price no longer compounds at each refit (finding 29). t1 is that baseline; it is read against batch 25's fix1 on the same runners (the stored predictions, paired offline) for what the rebuilt table is worth. t1_seed is t1 at seed 1 and t1_placebo adds ten columns of noise (greyhound/blocks/placebo.py): the two floors a gain must clear. t1_trials adds the trials table (greyhound/pit/trials.py: the trial form itself). t1_dyad and t1_cycle add the dyadic memory (rebuilt on the new expected times) and the season cycle. t1_notr drops the trainer-at-the-time columns (cx_tr_, cx_new_trainer, mk_tr_), which the audit found empty on the morning card and filled later the same day (findings 5 and 7): what they cost to lose. The bar: 3 bootstrap standard errors on the RMSE of log(BSP) against t1 and clear of both floors, the log-loss no worse beyond 1; each arm also read by period (1 Jun - 31 Aug, 1 Sep - 5 Nov: the audit's finding 4, the window has chosen the recipes it is quoted on) and by the runs behind the dog.",
